        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Do I need iFIT to use a ProForm treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. Every ProForm on this page works as a normal treadmill without a membership: you set speed and incline yourself. iFIT Train or iFIT Pro adds trainer-led classes that control the treadmill, SmartAdjust and ActivePulse, so pay for it only if you will use the classes.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Which ProForm treadmill is best for running?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The Carbon TLX at $849 on Amazon on 22 November 2026 is the cheapest ProForm here with a 12 mph top speed. The Carbon TL and TLS top out at 10 mph, which suits walking and light jogging rather than running.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much does a ProForm treadmill cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On Amazon on 22 November 2026, from $479 for the Carbon TL to $1,665.27 for the Pro 9000. The Carbon TLS was $559.30, the Carbon TLX $849, the Carbon Pro 2000 $1,199 and the Carbon Pro 9000 $1,599.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do you need iFIT to use a ProForm treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. Every ProForm works as a plain treadmill without a membership. iFIT unlocks the classes, SmartAdjust and ActivePulse: iFIT Train ($15 a month) on the Carbon models, iFIT Pro ($39 a month) on the touchscreen models.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the cheapest ProForm treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The Carbon TL, at $479 on Amazon on 22 November 2026. It tops out at 10 mph and 10% incline, so the $849 Carbon TLX is the cheaper choice for running.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is a ProForm treadmill over five years?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              From $479 with no membership to about $3,939 for a Carbon Pro 9000 plus five years of iFIT Pro at $39 a month, at November 2026 prices with no rises assumed.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is ProForm cheaper than NordicTrack?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Generally, yes. Both use iFIT, but ProForm's range starts at $479 on Amazon, while NordicTrack's Commercial 1750 was $1,999. NordicTrack's higher models add features such as decline and heavier frames.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Which ProForm treadmill is the best value?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For running without a touchscreen, the Carbon TLX at $849: 12 mph and 12% incline, with iFIT Train optional. For a touchscreen, the Carbon Pro 2000 at $1,199, if you plan to pay for iFIT Pro.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

